      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i need some help with a rejection email. We had a candidate, Marcus, who went all the way to the final round for a Senior DevOps role here in Austin. He's actually really talented and had great technical skills, especially with Kubernetes, but we ended up going with someone who had just a bit more experience with our specific cloud architecture. \n\nCan you help me draft something that's professional and polite, but makes it clear we aren't moving forward? I want to keep the door open for future roles because he's a strong candidate.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
