      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a draft for your rejection email to Marcus. It should be professional, acknowledge his strengths, and keep the door open for future opportunities.\n\n***\n\n**Subject: Update on the Senior DevOps Role at [Company Name]**\n\nDear Marcus,\n\nThank you so much for taking the time to interview for the Senior DevOps role and for sharing your impressive technical expertise with our team. We were genuinely impressed with your skills, especially your deep knowledge of Kubernetes. While your talent is undeniable, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose specific background aligned more closely with our immediate needs regarding our proprietary cloud architecture. We truly value the time you invested in this process, and we hope you'll keep us in mind for future roles.\n\n***\n\nThis strikes a good balance, offering genuine praise while clearly communicating the decision. It's polite, professional, and leaves a positive impression. Good luck with your hiring!",
      "source": "target",
